{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 200,
    "dDurationMs": 3733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ghost cities, trillions in distressed debt\nand the biggest bankruptcy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3933,
    "dDurationMs": 1300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in Chinese history."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5233,
    "dDurationMs": 4267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just five years ago, the world was\nobsessed with China's property collapse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9766,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But today, the headlines have moved on\nto incredibly advanced"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13733,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "electric vehicles,\nsolar dominance and hyper advanced robots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18033,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Leaving a massive question unanswered."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20833,
    "dDurationMs": 4167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What actually happened to China's\nmassive housing crisis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25266,
    "dDurationMs": 4034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has essentially been canceled\nby a massive boom in advanced industries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29366,
    "dDurationMs": 4867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or is it still there in the background,\nsilently dragging down China's economy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34400,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while the world is distracted\nby shiny new Chinese technologies?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38933,
    "dDurationMs": 2767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Answering\nthese questions was not easy, since"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41700,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "China is increasingly restricting the data\nthey share with the world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45833,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there are now two pieces"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47633,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of really exciting research\nthat I just had to share with you today."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51600,
    "dDurationMs": 3833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, a comprehensive new macro\neconomic paper was recently released"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55466,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that maps China's current trajectory\ndirectly against Japan's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59666,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "infamous property\nbust induced last decade."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63633,
    "dDurationMs": 3733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But before getting into that paper,\nwe first need to contextualize it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67366,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with worrying new data from China."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70833,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While we know from the experience\nof Japan, Europe and the US that massive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74533,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "housing busts\ncan cause so-called great depressions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78400,
    "dDurationMs": 4033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "great recessions, and even lost decades,\nif we look at China's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82433,
    "dDurationMs": 4267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "macroeconomic data, it's really weathered\nthe storm remarkably well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86933,
    "dDurationMs": 5767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While economic growth has slowed down\nfrom around 10% to 5% and more recently,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92800,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "4.5%, that's\nstill something that rivaling economies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97000,
    "dDurationMs": 3566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like Japan\nand the US can only dream about."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100833,
    "dDurationMs": 4133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, for China,\nthe main worry is not about low growth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104966,
    "dDurationMs": 3034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but rather about how sustainable\nthat growth is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108366,
    "dDurationMs": 2734,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You see, before 2022, property investment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111100,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was one of China's main engines of growth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114366,
    "dDurationMs": 3234,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But as you can see here,\nnot only has that growth turned"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117633,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "negative, it's getting worse each year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120800,
    "dDurationMs": 3966,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so far, 2026\nlooks like the worst year yet,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124766,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with property investment\nfalling by a whopping 16.2%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129500,
    "dDurationMs": 3966,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But property investment is part of overall\nfixed asset investment,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133500,
    "dDurationMs": 4666,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which also includes infrastructure\nand notably factory investments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138200,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And actually, after a Covid drop\nand subsequent recovery,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142700,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "growth in fixed asset\ninvestments has hovered around 4%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147700,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But worryingly,\nthis picture has now flipped fixed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150900,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "investments, which include infrastructure,\nproperty and factory investments,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154700,
    "dDurationMs": 5933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are now dragging down\ngrowth by 4.1% in 2026."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161033,
    "dDurationMs": 3067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in my opinion,\nthe bigger picture is even more worrying"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164100,
    "dDurationMs": 4033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because total fixed investments\nnow look like they have,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168133,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after years of almost exponential growth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171166,
    "dDurationMs": 2967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have genuinely plateaued."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174133,
    "dDurationMs": 3467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But of course, investment is\njust one of the three major"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177600,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "components of economic growth,\nalongside consumption and exports."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182400,
    "dDurationMs": 4033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This brings us to the second piece\nof worrying data, which is that,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186700,
    "dDurationMs": 3866,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while, Chinese consumer spending\nwas growing relatively slowly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190566,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from our Chinese perspective,\nat about 3% after the real estate bust."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195566,
    "dDurationMs": 5134,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This has now turned negative in May,\nwhich only happened"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201300,
    "dDurationMs": 2433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the last couple of years during Covid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203733,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the other hand, as most of the world\nknows all too well, Chinese"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207133,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exports are still absolutely exploding."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211333,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, the problem for China\nis that it is now so big"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214533,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it cannot really export\nits way out of trouble."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217800,
    "dDurationMs": 4133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because if we look at the composition\nof Chinese GDP historically,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221933,
    "dDurationMs": 3533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even though China, we all know\nhas been an exporting powerhouse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225866,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are gray bars at the top."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227566,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They represent exports."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229366,
    "dDurationMs": 4867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is just a minor minor\nfraction of China's total economy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 234733,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, local consumption,\nwhich has been falling and investments,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240266,
    "dDurationMs": 4334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are far more important\nfor the Chinese economy as a whole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245200,
    "dDurationMs": 5666,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if we see that now both investment\nin total and consumption is negative,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251100,
    "dDurationMs": 2366,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's really something\nto worry about."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253466,
    "dDurationMs": 1767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what's causing it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255233,
    "dDurationMs": 3867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, we know that Chinese industry\nis still stronger than ever."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259466,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we know from history\nthat massive housing busts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262666,
    "dDurationMs": 4034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can suppress economic growth for years,\nif not decades."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267000,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So Chinese property\ninvestments getting worse and worse,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270433,
    "dDurationMs": 1433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more negative and more negative,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271866,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is actually a really strong signal\nthat the property crisis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274966,
    "dDurationMs": 4034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is not just still ongoing,\nbut that it may actually be getting worse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279233,
    "dDurationMs": 1367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is what it looks like."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280600,
    "dDurationMs": 1566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But is that actually the case?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282166,
    "dDurationMs": 2834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is China's housing crisis to blame?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285000,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This gets us to a new, detailed paper\non the Chinese housing bubble"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289800,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is called a Tale of Two Countries: the real estate crises in 1990s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294200,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Japan and contemporary China,\nwhere Harvard professor Kenneth Rogoff"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298500,
    "dDurationMs": 5833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and IMF economist Yuanchen Yang\nnot only present new, super detailed city"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304333,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "level data on China's housing crisis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307233,
    "dDurationMs": 4133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They also compare that to new super\ndetailed data from Japan's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311400,
    "dDurationMs": 1166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "property bust."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312566,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how exactly has China's housing\ncrisis been going?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315833,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As you can see here, it's still ongoing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318433,
    "dDurationMs": 4167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is no sign of prices\nstabilizing or coming back up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322600,
    "dDurationMs": 4266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And notably,\nsecond-tier cities like Xiamen,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 327133,
    "dDurationMs": 2967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Quanzhou, Xiangyang, and Zhengzhou."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330100,
    "dDurationMs": 4833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I've seen an almost 30%\ndrop in house prices since their peak."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335033,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, top tier\ncities like Beijing and Shanghai"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339000,
    "dDurationMs": 4466,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hidden over there have only seen\na 10% reduction in house prices so far."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343500,
    "dDurationMs": 3033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Comparing that to less detailed\ndata on Japan's housing bust,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346533,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where house prices\ndropped to around 40% of their peak."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351533,
    "dDurationMs": 4867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The authors conclude that if China's\nadjustment unfolds in a similar way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356400,
    "dDurationMs": 5333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as Japan, it would mean China has not gone\nhalf way through the transition."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 362133,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But by contrast,\nif China's path is eventually comparable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365733,
    "dDurationMs": 4067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the United States,\nit appears to have already covered roughly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370066,
    "dDurationMs": 3634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "two thirds of the adjustment\nbefore reaching the bottom."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373900,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what does that mean for China's\neconomy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376200,
    "dDurationMs": 4666,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is a Japan style, decade long stagnation\nstill the most likely scenario,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380900,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or should we expect a swift bounce back\nin just a few years?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385033,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As we saw in the United States, to answer\nthat question, Rogoff and Yang identified"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389766,
    "dDurationMs": 3567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "three channels through\nwhich housing busts affect the economy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393600,
    "dDurationMs": 3633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If there is no credit crunch,\nand that's a big if,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397233,
    "dDurationMs": 4533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you see, as various research papers\nhave shown, after the 2007 crisis,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402133,
    "dDurationMs": 2667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Western banks\nseverely restricted borrowing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404800,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to firms right after 2007 helped\nturn an asset bust"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409033,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into what we now know\nas the Great Recession."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413166,
    "dDurationMs": 3134,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, if we look at Chinese bank\nlending data, we can see that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 416300,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while Chinese state owned banks did slowly\nreduce lending to the property sector,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421866,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they increased lending\nto the advanced industries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 425566,
    "dDurationMs": 6667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that dominate the news cycle today\nby massive amounts, almost 40%,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432666,
    "dDurationMs": 4967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and therefore overall lending growth\nremained positive around 10%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437666,
    "dDurationMs": 3867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's very different than what happened\nduring the Great Recession in the West."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441733,
    "dDurationMs": 5067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if unlike the US after 2007,\nChina did not experience a credit crisis,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 446800,
    "dDurationMs": 4033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but rather a credit shift\nfrom property to manufacturing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450833,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then why are both investment\nand consumption now in so much trouble?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456100,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This brings us to the three non-financial\nchannels described by Rogoff and Yang."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461233,
    "dDurationMs": 3467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First,\nthere's this so-called investment channel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465066,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And to understand how this works,\nhave a look at this graph."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468300,
    "dDurationMs": 3566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, the blue lines\nshow residential real estate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471866,
    "dDurationMs": 4067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "investment over GDP in Japan,\nwhich peaked in the 1980s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 475933,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and 1990s at around 6%,\nafter which they dropped to 3%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481300,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, the red bars\nrepresent Chinese property investment,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 485133,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which shot up much faster from about 2%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 489133,
    "dDurationMs": 4133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in 97 to about 10% in 2020."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 493400,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Today, it has already dropped to about 5%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 498066,
    "dDurationMs": 2134,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, if you follow the logic\nof the investment channel,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 500200,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then less property investment\nis really bad for the economy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503300,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because it means less business\nfor architects,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 505600,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "less business for builders, realtors,\nkitchen sellers, electricians,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509700,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "furniture shops and so on and so on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512700,
    "dDurationMs": 4533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as we have seen, negative property\ninvestment was definitely a huge drag"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517233,
    "dDurationMs": 5133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the Chinese economy for the past years,\nbut so far it has been offset"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522600,
    "dDurationMs": 2766,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by a massive investment\nboom in manufacturing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 525366,
    "dDurationMs": 3834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meaning that total investment\nremains positive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529700,
    "dDurationMs": 3066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "until this year, when property investments\nwere worse than ever."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533033,
    "dDurationMs": 3933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And at the same time, China's\nleadership started its so-called anti"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536966,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "involution campaign,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538566,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is an effort by the government\nto curb hyper competition and overcapacity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542766,
    "dDurationMs": 3667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in crowded sectors\nlike solar and EV manufacturing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 546600,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which meant that local governments\nhad to reduce excessive investments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550000,
    "dDurationMs": 5066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the sectors that they had previously\nmade to hit their GDP growth targets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 555533,
    "dDurationMs": 1967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it gets worse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 557500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The second channel through\nwhich housing busts affect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561000,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the economy\nis that a lot of households used to save"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564500,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the future via\nhaving a second or third property."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568433,
    "dDurationMs": 3667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as house prices went up, households\nfelt rich and therefore"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572100,
    "dDurationMs": 3466,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were confident that they could afford\nto spend more and more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 575800,
    "dDurationMs": 3566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, now that housing prices\nare dropping for years, households"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 579366,
    "dDurationMs": 4934,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are actually seeing their wealth shrink\nand therefore logically are spending less."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 584833,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is called the consumption channel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587133,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Finally,\nthe authors show that in Japan, areas"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591100,
    "dDurationMs": 3533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where housing prices dropped\nfastest households also became"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 594633,
    "dDurationMs": 4433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "increasingly pessimistic,\nreducing their consumption even more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 599266,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they call this the sentiment channel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 601966,
    "dDurationMs": 3767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And using a large language model,\nthey see that the same effect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 605733,
    "dDurationMs": 4233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is clearly happening in China as well,\nespecially in second"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 609966,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tier cities where the housing crisis\nhas hit the hardest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613033,
    "dDurationMs": 4533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Consumers are increasingly pessimistic\nabout China's economic future."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 617966,
    "dDurationMs": 4467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, in conclusion,\nhow has China's housing bust been going?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 622733,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, it's still very much ongoing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625533,
    "dDurationMs": 4667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But because China shifted\nto a massive manufacturing boom"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630200,
    "dDurationMs": 4466,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in investment and lending via its state\nowned banks, we have not seen the effects"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 634666,
    "dDurationMs": 5134,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as strongly yet as Japan in the 1990s\nor the US after 2007."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 639833,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now that China's anti-inflation\ncampaign is reining"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 643033,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in manufacturing lending,\nwe are starting to see the macroeconomic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 647233,
    "dDurationMs": 3633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "effects of China's property\nbust more clearly again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 651200,
    "dDurationMs": 1300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how long will that take?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652500,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Will China's housing bust\nbe more like the US, Japan or worse?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 657566,
    "dDurationMs": 3567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Given that the US private banks\ncleared that that much more quickly,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 661133,
    "dDurationMs": 1167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think the answer is that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 662300,
    "dDurationMs": 3466,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "China's housing bust\nwill probably be more like that of Japan."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 666233,
    "dDurationMs": 2767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if China's housing bust will play out\nlike Japan,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 669000,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can expect another six years\nof lackluster consumption."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 673500,
    "dDurationMs": 3433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if the anti-inflation\ncampaign continues, we can now expect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677100,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much worse\ninvestment growth in China as well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 680400,
    "dDurationMs": 3633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "China's strategy has been so far\nto rely on manufacturing investments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684300,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to compensate for this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 685700,
    "dDurationMs": 4033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But with households suffering from\nthe real estate bust unable to buy enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 689733,
    "dDurationMs": 5700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "solar panels, EVs and robots, this excess\nproduction inevitably was sent overseas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696000,
    "dDurationMs": 4533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if we look at China's massive economy,\nwe can clearly see the problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700800,
    "dDurationMs": 3866,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "China is simply too big to rely on exports"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704900,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to get out of this economic crisis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 707966,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So with the manufacturing investment boom\ncoming to an end, I think it's likely"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 711566,
    "dDurationMs": 1634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the world will again"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713200,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have to start worrying about China's\ncontinuing housing crisis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 717366,
    "dDurationMs": 3034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for a more detailed\ndive into the other side of its economy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 720400,
    "dDurationMs": 4633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its high tech success and export success,\nI highly recommend you check out some key"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 725100,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "follow up articles from our advertising\nsponsor, The Economist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 729433,
    "dDurationMs": 2833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Specifically,\nstart with a deep dive on how"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732266,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "big China's emerging industries\nactually are."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 735766,
    "dDurationMs": 1167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then follow up with this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736933,
    "dDurationMs": 3867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "deep dive on how these industries\ncompare to China's old economy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 740833,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And finally,\nthis take on why China's export success"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 744133,
    "dDurationMs": 4467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is making a trade war\nbetween the EU and China seem inevitable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 748966,
    "dDurationMs": 3034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As these analysis show,\nThe Economist delivers insights"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752000,
    "dDurationMs": 2233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that truly help\nyou see the bigger picture."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 754233,
    "dDurationMs": 3933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is why I highly recommend\nyou subscribe to The Economist, which now"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 758166,
    "dDurationMs": 4134,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "offers an exclusive 35% discount\nfor many macro viewers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 762700,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whether you prefer your daily journalism\nin The Economist app"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 765966,
    "dDurationMs": 3167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or you're like me and enjoy\ncatching up on the global economy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 769133,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over the weekend with a cup of coffee\nand the print edition,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 772766,
    "dDurationMs": 4234,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you'll always stay on top of the latest\nglobal developments and support journalism"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 777000,
    "dDurationMs": 4533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that values factual information, integrity\nand an independent point of view."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 781900,
    "dDurationMs": 1266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So don't miss out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 783166,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Click a link in the description\nor top comment below, or head"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 786466,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over to economist.com/money Macro to claim"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 789666,
    "dDurationMs": 3834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your exclusive 35% discount today."
    } ]
  } ]
}
